 programs, the application dates are only for the CS affiliated application. For the Graduate School of Business and School of Law application deadlines, please refer to the respective websites for additional information.\nFor the CS Coterminal program, you are only allowed to apply for a maximum of 3 attempts.\nProgram\nEntry quarter\nApplication opens\nApplication deadline\nDecision\ndate\nPhD Application\nAutumn\nSeptember 15, 2026\nDecember 8, 2026\nFebruary 2027\nMaster's Application\nAutumn\nSeptember 15, 2026\nDecember 8, 2026\nMarch 2027\nCoterm Application (Stanford undergraduates only)\nWinter 2026-2027\nSeptember 22, 2026\nOctober 6, 2026\nOctober 30, 2026\nSpring 2026-2027\nDecember 15, 2026\nJanuary 8, 2027\nJanuary 29, 2027\nAutumn 2027-2028\nApril 9, 2027\nApril 30, 2027\nMay 27, 2027\nCS MS/MBA Application\n(CS MS deadline only)\nAutumn\nSeptember 15, 2026\nDecember 8, 2026\nMarch 2026\nCS MS/Law Application\n(CS MS deadline only)\nAutumn\nSeptember 15, 2026\nDecember 8, 2026\nMarch 2027\nCS PhD/Law Application\n(CS PhD deadline only)\nAutumn\nSeptember 15, 2026\nDecember 8, 2026\nFebruary 2027\nKHS Deadline\nThe Knight-Hennessy Scholars (KHS) is a prestigious scholarship program. It is designed to build a multidisciplinary community of Stanford graduate students dedicated to finding creative solutions to the world's greatest challenges. KHS admits up to 100 high-achieving students every year from across Stanford's seven (7) graduate schools. Scholars receive up to three (3) years of full funding for graduate studies at Stanford.\nCandidates of any country may apply. KHS applicants must have earned their first undergraduate degree within the last seven years, and must apply to both a Stanford graduate program (MS or PhD) and to KHS.\nThe application closes on October 6, 2026, at 1 pm, Pacific Time to join their 2027 Fall Cohort. Learn More.\nTOEFL/IELTS Deadline\nOctober 2026 (at least six weeks before the application deadline) is the suggested deadline to ensure scores are received in time for review.\nCS Graduate Application\nApplicants to graduate studies in Computer Science must apply either to MS (including HCP) or PhD, not to both.\nApply to the graduate program\nCS Coterm Application\nApplicants to the CS Coterm program must be a current Stanford undergraduate. Students on leave of absence are not eligible to apply.\nApply to the Coterm program\nBack to Top\nThe CS Intranet: Resources for Faculty, Staff, and Current Students\nFor Faculty & Staff\nFor Current CS Students\nIntranet\nWeb Login\nAddress\nGates Computer Science Building\n353 Jane Stanford Way\nStanford, CA 94305\nUnited States\nContact Us\nDirections to the Gates Building\nCampus Map\nFollow us on LinkedIn\nLinks to\nEvents\nStanford Engineering News\nStudent Resources\nCS IT Support\nCS Student Resources\nComputer Forum | Career Readiness\nEngineering Entrepreneurship Center\nSERIS Program\nTerman Engineering Library\nStanford\nUniversity\nStanford Home\nMaps & Directions\nSearch Stanford\nEmergency Info\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy\nCopyright\nTrademarks\nNon-Discrimination\nAccessibility\n\u00a9 Stanford University.\nStanford, California 94305.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/admissions-graduate-application-deadlines#main-content"], ["Skip to secondary navigation", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/admissions-graduate-application-deadlines#secondary-navigation"], ["Stanford University", "https://www.stanford.edu"], ["Stanford Engineering Computer Science Engineering", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/"], ["Home", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/home"], ["About", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/about"], ["Gates Building", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/about/gates-computer-science-building"], ["Work Here", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/about/careers-work-us"], ["Academics & Students", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/academics-and-students"], ["Academics", "https://www.cs.stanford.edu/academics-overview"], ["Bachelor's", "https://www.